.TH KURENAI 1 "2026-11-14" "kurenai 3.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kurenai \- neon-red system information panel for the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kurenai
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kurenai
prints a compact panel with system, hardware, performance and memory
information: kernel, shell, uptime, CPU, GPU, LAN and public IP,
temperature, load, RAM, swap, disk, battery and a CPU sparkline.
.PP
Everything is read from
.IR /proc ,
.IR /sys ,
.BR df (1),
.BR lspci (8)
and
.BR nvidia-smi (1).
The panel is written in Bash and has no runtime dependencies beyond the
standard utilities.
.PP
It can run once, for example from a shell startup file, or stay open as a
live monitor that redraws every second.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-refresh
Ignore the public IP cache and query the address again.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-no\-net
Do not query the public IP.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-no\-anim
Disable the animation and print a static panel.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-time " " \fIS\fR
Animation length in seconds. Accepts a decimal comma. The default is 0.3;
0 disables the animation.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-monitor
Live monitor mode. Requires an interactive terminal.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interval " " \fIS\fR
Monitor refresh interval in seconds, between 0.25 and 10. Implies
.BR \-m .
.TP
.BR \-\-frames " " \fIN\fR
Render
.I N
frames and exit. Intended for tests.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-lang " " \fIL\fR
Output language:
.B es
or
.BR en .
The default is taken from the locale.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the help and exit.
.SH MONITOR KEYS
.TP
.B q
Quit and restore the terminal.
.TP
.B p
Pause or resume data collection.
.TP
.B +
Increase the refresh interval by 0.25 seconds.
.TP
.B \-
Decrease the refresh interval by 0.25 seconds.
.TP
.B r
Refresh static data and the public IP.
.TP
.B h
Show or hide the help footer.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-C
Quit and restore the terminal.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B KURENAI_LANG
Force the language,
.B es
or
.BR en .
.TP
.B KURENAI_NO_NET
If set to 1, do not query the public IP. Same as
.BR \-n .
.TP
.B KURENAI_NO_ANIM
If set to 1, disable the animation. Same as
.BR \-q .
.TP
.B KURENAI_ACCENT
Main color as three RGB components, for example
.RB \(dq0 255 180\(dq.
Defaults to
.RB \(dq255 0 0\(dq.
.TP
.B KURENAI_BAR_W
Bar width, from 4 to 14. Defaults to 10.
.TP
.B KURENAI_WIDTH
Force the panel width, from 40 to 84. Useful for tests and screenshots.
.TP
.B KURENAI_INTERVAL
Default monitor interval in seconds.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
If set, disable all color output.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.cache/kurenai/public-ip
Cached public IP address, created with mode 600 and valid for 15 minutes.
The location follows
.BR XDG_CACHE_HOME .
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B kurenai
Print the panel with the default animation.
.TP
.B kurenai \-m \-i 2
Monitor the system with a two second refresh interval.
.TP
.B KURENAI_ACCENT="0 255 180" kurenai
Print the panel with a teal accent.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid option, invalid argument, or monitor mode without an interactive
terminal.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR df (1),
.BR free (1),
.BR top (1)
